27%&amp;#10;It rained 19% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"152.1927027027027\" cy=\"313.1351351351351\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 55%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"251.16776119402982\" cy=\"316.80597014925377\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 77%&amp;#10;It rained 42% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"330.2890410958904\" cy=\"227.4246575342466\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 92%&amp;#10;It rained 54% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"383.5773913043478\" cy=\"186.81159420289853\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 75% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 147 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.08489795918365\" cy=\"109.61904761904759\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(29%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Khulna the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.19) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-2.48).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>167</td><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'>-2.475</td><td class='num'>3.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>209</td><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'>-0.612</td><td class='num'>26.3%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>159</td><td class='num'>69%</td><td class='num'>0.081</td><td class='num'>18.8%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.188</td><td class='num'>16.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":22.80979,"lon":89.56439,"n":710,"n_cities":216,"name":"Khulna","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":212,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.05750000000000001,"n":68,"obs":0.04411764705882353,"sig":false},{"hi":0.44,"lo":0.14,"mean":0.26608108108108103,"n":74,"obs":0.1891891891891892,"sig":false},{"hi":0.67,"lo":0.44,"mean":0.5456716417910447,"n":67,"obs":0.1791044776119403,"sig":true},{"hi":0.86,"lo":0.67,"mean":0.7691780821917809,"n":73,"obs":0.4246575342465753,"sig":true},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.86,"mean":0.9197101449275362,"n":69,"obs":0.5362318840579711,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9974149659863946,"n":147,"obs":0.7482993197278912,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":4.3,"provisional":false,"rank":166,"rank_hi":196.0,"rank_lo":86.975,"reliability":0.05265735758830582,"resolution":0.08436259089813111,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"khulna","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Dhaka"}